 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 531960,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Consider the following examples.\n The toxicity in the venom from a Brazilian viper (Bothropsjararaca) is due to a sudden, massive drop in blood pressure, which slows down the reaction of a bitten prey.\n Solutions made from the opium poppy have been used in the past to dull the sensation of pain and induces a sense of wellbeing.\n How can the effects of these natural compounds be applied to the development of medical treatments?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1040756,
     "content_html": "Compounds similar to the snake’s active toxin are used routinely as antivirals. Opioids are used as immunomodulators, which modifies an immune response."
    },
    {
     "id": 1040757,
     "content_html": "Compounds similar to the snake’s active toxin are used routinely as painkillers. Opioids help in the lowering of blood pressure."
    },
    {
     "id": 1040758,
     "content_html": "Compounds similar to the snake’s active toxin are used to treat inflammations. Opioids are used to prevent muscle spasms."
    },
    {
     "id": 1040759,
     "content_html": "Compounds similar to the snake’s active toxin are used to lower blood pressure. Opioids are used routinely as painkillers."
    }
   ],
